{"agent":"impl-complete-lint-exempt","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`complete` normalises `lint_exempt` with `.strip()` when deciding whether a lint exemption was supplied, but `_close_bugs` forwards the raw value to `bug_fixed`. Given `complete(repo, \"fix-BUG\", regression_test=\"tests/test_a.py\", lint_exempt=\"   \")`, `closing` and the failure flag treat `lint_exempt` as absent (the reason string is whitespace), yet `_close_bugs` calls `bug_fixed(..., lint_exempt=\"   \")`. A whitespace-only value is not a lint-exempt reason, so the downstream call receives a non-empty exemption string that the caller did not actually supply; if `bug_fixed` uses the natural truthiness check for a reason string, this can trigger the lint-exempt path or a lint-exempt refusal even though `complete` considered no exemption to have been given. The value forwarded should be normalised (e.g. pass `lint_exempt.strip()`, or pass `\"\"` when it is blank).","digest":"e8eea4de1309221a","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/complete.py:_close_bugs","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/complete.py:_close_bugs"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Replacing `regression_test=tests if any(t.strip() for t in tests) else []` with `regression_test=tests` forwards an all-blank regression-test list unchanged. `complete`’s gate treats `[\"\"]` as “no regression test” because it checks `any(t.strip() ...)`, but `_close_bugs` now calls `bug_fixed(..., regression_test=[\"\"], lint_exempt=\"formatted\")`. The previous code deliberately collapsed that case to `[]` so `bug_fixed` would take the lint-exempt path and record the exemption reason (as asserted by the existing `regression_verify.reason == \"formatted\"` test). With `bug_fixed` unchanged in this diff, a non-empty list containing only an empty string is still a supplied regression test, so a lint-only completion can be recorded against a bogus blank test instead of the lint-exempt reason.","digest":"e27625dcb49a0d2d","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/complete.py:_close_bugs","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/complete.py:_close_bugs"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The added test does not actually guard the fix. For `regression_test=[\"\"], lint_exempt=\"formatted\"`, the pre-diff code also succeeded: it converted `[\"\"]` to `[]` and forwarded the non-empty `lint_exempt`. It also does not exercise the whitespace-only `lint_exempt` case that motivated the previous finding, nor does it assert the `bug.fixed` event’s `regression_verify.reason`. Thus it would not fail on the unfixed code and would not catch a regression of the lint-exempt normalization.","digest":"b10eae442931d62c","location":"tests/test_complete_lint_exempt.py:54","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_complete_lint_exempt.py:54"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":0,"delta_from":"4c15ac2bb0173ee9e290fa54937e068532dd1ff3","delta_raised":[],"delta_rounds":2,"diff_chars":918,"diff_sha":"36b875521eb0e10d0d199aabca38d381fa8b97739afc92f95bf980c53d09901d","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 4c15ac2bb0","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":337.0,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"full_coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Be5610bf732.critic.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261029T194617Z-f3a7fac2.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"8432f27b390a205727689e21ca6566c865a50649","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/complete.py":"100644 328c08c9439b3feea8785808cbc987ea2ef1cbbd","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle.py":"100644 9af28e08db414d0048f385e855005dd23fd83121","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 3d725457a6cd4aa6810909567afb66e00ecb3f14","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr":"100644 7f96f94fa5ddac1564dcd46bc9